-- title:
--   Logarithmic band covolume in a twisted centralizer of a scalar class
-- statement:
--   Let $K$ and $L$ be number fields with $L/K$ finite Galois, and let $\sigma \in \mathrm{Gal}(L/K)$ be such that every $K$-automorphism of $L$ lies in $\langle \sigma \rangle$ (so the group is cyclic, generated by $\sigma$). Let $\delta_0, h \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L)$ and $d \in L^{\times}$ satisfy $h^{-1}\,\delta_0\,\sigma(h) = d\cdot 1$, where $\sigma$ acts entrywise; that is, $\delta_0$ is $\sigma$-twisted conjugate over $L$ to a scalar matrix. Let $c$ be a unit of $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ and put $\delta = (\delta_0 \otimes 1)\cdot (c \cdot 1)$ in $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$, the first factor being the image of $\delta_0$ under $\ell \mapsto \ell \otimes 1$ applied entrywise. Let $T' = \{\,t : t\,\delta\,\sigma(t)^{-1} = \delta\,\}$ be the $\sigma$-twisted centralizer of $\delta$, where $\sigma$ acts on $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K$ through the first factor and entrywise on matrices; $T'$ carries the subspace topology with its Borel structure, and $\tau'$ is a Haar measure on $T'$. Then there is a constant $C \in [0,\infty]$ with $C \neq 0$ and $C \neq \infty$ such that for every subset $D' \subseteq T'$ which is a $\tau'$-fundamental domain for the right translation action on $T'$ of the subgroup $\Gamma' = \{\,g \in \mathrm{GL}_2(L) : g\,\delta_0\,\sigma(g)^{-1} = \delta_0\,\}$, pushed into $\mathrm{GL}_2(L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K)$ by $\ell \mapsto \ell \otimes 1$ and viewed as a subgroup of $T'$, and for all reals $0 < a \le b$, $$\tau'\bigl(D' \cap \{\, t : \lVert \det t \rVert_L \in [a,b] \,\}\bigr) = C \cdot \log(b/a).$$ Here $\det t$ is computed after transporting $t$ along the ring isomorphism $L \otimes_K \mathbb{A}_K \cong \mathbb{A}_K \otimes_K L \cong \mathbb{A}_L$ (commutativity of the tensor product followed by the canonical base-change identification of adele rings), and $\lVert \cdot \rVert_L$ is the idele norm of $L$, defined as the module of multiplication by the given idele on $\mathbb{A}_L$ for the Haar measure.
--
--   This is the finiteness, non-vanishing and logarithmic dependence on the band $a \le \lVert \det t\rVert_L \le b$ of the covolume of the $L$-rational twisted centralizer inside the adelic twisted centralizer, for a class whose norm is central in the strong sense that $\delta_0$ is $\sigma$-twisted conjugate to a scalar; such a twisted centralizer is a form of $\mathrm{GL}_2$ over $K$, and the constant $C$ is the measure-theoretic input to the contribution of these classes in the twisted trace formula for cyclic base change of $\mathrm{GL}_2$. It is used in the evaluation of integrals over a fundamental domain in the twisted centralizer against the value at the central scalar.
